 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(V \cdot T)$ for a mesh with $T$ triangles and $V$ voxels, assuming brute-force search. Spatial acceleration structures (BVH, grid) can reduce this to $O(V \log T)$ or better [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V)$ for the TSDF volume, where $V$ is the number of voxels. Sparse representations can reduce this significantly [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
 *   **Strengths:** Directly handles explicit geometry; robust to non-watertight surfaces with the offset fallback; compatible with compression pipelines designed for TSDF [S1].
 *   **Limitations:** Computationally expensive for high-resolution meshes without acceleration; sign ambiguity for non-watertight surfaces requires fallback [S1].
